WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.710
A great and vast ocean of words.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.480
Standing in front of this ocean,

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.710
without a means to cross the ocean,

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.680
we can only stand and watch.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.450
However,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.720
when a ship is completed,

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.020
you will be able to embark
on an unimaginable journey.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.260
You can express these words
and feelings inside you,

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.560
freeing them from deep within you.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.760
And...

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:35.440
to go on a journey to receive
the thoughts and words of another.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.320
The Great Passage

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.120
A quiet dreamlike morning
The madder red sky

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.630
Shines through the window
And reflects on my pen

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:04.800
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.630
Deep thoughts, flexible conception

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.370
Foreseeable aspirations
Distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:17.810
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.250
The light in our eyes
That differ from each other

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.380
Traces of friendship
That’s not in the treaty

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:30.660
In the ocean that sweeps
The sand of eternity

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:37.730
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:44.200
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.770
Reference, conclusion

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:50.780
I’ll gather words that have
Scattered over many months and years

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.880
The fragrant sea breeze

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:57.180
The connection that rests on the seashore
Become one.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.160
Compile

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.810
Really? Here?

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.360
Dictionary Editorial Department

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:48.430
No, that's not it.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.540
Excuse me.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.180
Is there anyone here?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.950
Oh, we've been waiting for you.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.850
I'm...

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.350
We know.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.960
- Chief. Chief Majime.
- Yes, I'm over here.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.760
- She's here.
- What?

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.560
The girl starting today.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.530
Oh, that's right!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.740
Please hold on one moment.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.470
I'm so sorry.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.440
I'm Mitsuya Majime.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.840
Business card?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.520
I'm Kishibe.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:38.350
I'm from the Northern Black
Editorial Team.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.850
I'm transferring into this department
starting today.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.360
Pleased to meet you.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.890
Yes, pleased to meet you.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.900
Let's see, we should first...

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.870
This is the Dictionary
Editorial Department.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.800
The only company employees here
are me and you, Kishibe-san.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.770
I'm Sasaki.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.540
I'm a contract worker.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.380
Um...

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.010
Then are there only three people here?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.420
Occasionally, we have a professor
who is supervising the dictionary

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:11.520
and another part-time worker.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.750
Occasionally?

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.520
Is there a problem?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.860
No, I'm just surprised.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.960
Feel free to take any desk you like.
That's all right, isn't it, Majime-san?

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.960
Yes, you can use any desk.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.470
Thank you very much.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.500
Um...

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:31.970
Where should I...?

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.310
Oh, no!

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.610
I'm so sorry to ask you after just arriving,

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.880
but could you start
with clearing them off?

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.350
Yes, I understand.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.760
I'll be in the archive room.
Come get me if you need anything.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:52.990
Okay.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.870
No, that's not right

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.500
Time to roll up my sleeves!

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.760
Socket Booster Encyclopedia

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.880
The feeling of "away-kan" is strong here.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.450
Kishibe-san.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.820
What does "away-kan" mean?

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.750
You just used this phrase "away-kan,"
didn't you?

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:56.360
Yes.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.520
- What is that?
- What is this?

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.730
Do you mean the meaning?

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:08.400
Like you feel out of place.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:10.600
Or it's like you're a little lonely.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.970
Or a feeling of alienation?

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.870
So it's "away" in katakana?

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:17.680
And "kan" is like for feeling?
Is that right?

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.750
That's right

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.680
What other meanings are there?

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:23.980
Other?

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.890
Other

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.460
You feel like you're in the middle
of the enemy camp.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:35.560
- Enemy camp.
- Or like my situation now.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.870
You're wrong, Kishibe-san.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.840
I mean, by wrong...

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.440
I don't mean your meaning.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:50.410
In any case, this isn't the enemy camp
for you.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:51.540
But I...

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.080
I've been at a fashion magazine
my whole career.

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.180
Now suddenly I have
to write a dictionary?

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.750
I can't imagine I'm even cut out for it.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.120
There doesn't seem to be anything
I could even do.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.920
That's not true.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.930
You are very suited
for editing dictionaries.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.460
See?

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.700
It's incredible.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.200
I think anybody could do that.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.100
Oh, how do I say this?

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.540
It's so tidy and neat.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.440
Dictionary making
is about keeping things in order.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.510
It's a job about organizing words in a--

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.680
I'll just continue with the rest.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.660
I'm here again today.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.640
Excuse me!

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:57.180
We've been looking forward to this.
Kishibe-san.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:00.480
This is Miyamoto-san
from Akebono Papers.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.780
Could you also come here for a second?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.950
Yes, of course.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:09.520
I made this to match the total number
of pages for Daitokai that we chose.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.560
Please look through and check it.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.960
Thank you.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.830
What is that?

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.940
I just transferred here yesterday.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:26.870
Oh, is that so?

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:29.510
I was wondering why I hadn't seen you
around before.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:34.150
What Majime-san is looking through now
is a sample for Daitokai.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.580
- Daitokai?
- Yes.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.020
That's the new mid-sized dictionary
being made here.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:44.860
This paper was specially developed
just for Daitokai.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:49.130
A new type of paper is created
just for a dictionary?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:54.730
Yes. Daitokai is planning
on containing 240,000 entries.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:58.800
But the book must be held
under three inches.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.910
By developing a special new paper,

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:04.280
you can have more pages while keeping
the same thickness, meaning

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.210
you can include more words.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:07.980
I see.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.580
230,000 entries was the limit previously,

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:15.150
but with some innovation we were able
to increase that by 10,000.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.290
Amazing.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.860
Just making it thin will result in paper
that tears easily.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.660
But this paper is thin yet still strong

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.100
while staying light weight.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.770
What's more, you can't see
through the pages.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.140
It took us some time to get to this place,

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.840
but I'm very proud of it.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:37.980
Paper has just been something you picked
from an existing lineup,

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.150
but you made it from the ground up.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.080
This won't work.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.260
- It's lacking a stickiness.
- Stickiness?

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.790
- Excuse me!
- Kishibe-san.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:56.230
Please thumb through the Kojien
dictionary we have there.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:01.100
Does it not feel like the paper just sticks
to your fingers?

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:09.040
It sticks to your finger, yet it does not stick
to the next page either.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.240
That is the stickiness.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:14.650
What is so wrong with this?

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:18.080
I think this sample is plenty easy
to thumb through.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.250
It's not good enough.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.220
Dictionaries are thick books.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:25.220
Flipping through them
should not feel stressful.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.990
I'm terribly sorry.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.200
It does lack sufficient stickiness.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.060
I will remake it right away.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:33.070
Please.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.300
Thank you.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.970
I will have our technicians go over it
right away.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.140
We will make a new sample.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.070
Dictionaries are so...

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:51.860
- Thank you for this meal.
- Thank you for this meal.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.370
This is for you, Torao-san.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:59.770
I got this asparagus from the market.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.110
How is it?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.480
- Micchan?
- Oh, I'm sorry.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.910
I was just doing some thinking.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.420
About which definition?

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.320
Oh, it's not about a definition.

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:17.890
I was just wondering what I can do to help
me understand young women better.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:20.090
She's a new transfer.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.200
You know. I mentioned her before.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:25.000
So she finally came.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.370
Did you throw her a welcome party?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.470
Not yet. Of course! A welcome party.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.840
Will your VIP room be free tomorrow?

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.380
It will be free tomorrow.

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:38.510
- If you could...
- Got it.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.480
- But Micchan...
- Yes?

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:45.020
I would try to phrase it
so there isn't any misunderstanding.

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:47.950
Not that I think you can.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.360
What? Oh! I'm sorry.

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.300
This is very good.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.000
I forgive you.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:09.510
That is how Daitokai was started.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:16.480
Kishibe-san. We are very honored
to welcome you to our family.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.290
Although, I'm the only employee...

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.490
Why is your speech so long?!

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.090
Why are you even here?!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.090
Why wouldn't I be?!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.560
I have to check out the new girl for myself!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.530
Thank you all for this party.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:32.970
Kishibe-san.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:36.070
This is Matsumoto-sensei
we mentioned yesterday

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:38.800
who is supervising our dictionary for us.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.340
I'm Matsumoto.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:41.840
I'm Kishibe.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:43.510
And this is Araki-san.

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.440
He was originally an employee,

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.850
but he comes part-time now.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:50.950
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.850
And this is Nishioka-san.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:56.420
He will show up for dinners like tonight.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.460
That's all my introduction is?!

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.130
Oh, was that not right?

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:04.400
You could mention so many other things.
Like being the hottest guy in PR.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.330
Right, Kishibe-chan?

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:10.070
Are you used to dictionary work yet?

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.570
No, since I haven't done anything yet.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:14.510
He's kind of different, you know?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:18.010
Anyway, there will surely be challenges,
but good luck.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.250
What do you mean that I'm different?

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:22.480
You're different!

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:26.090
You were told the Socket Boom
Encyclopedia they forced on you

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:27.850
could be something simple.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:31.160
But you turned it
into a real character encyclopedia.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.430
- Socket Boom? You mean the game?
- Yes!

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.130
We're doing that all for Daitokai.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:42.600
Kishibe, the company sees us
as a real money hog.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.070
That's why we have to do things
like revise other dictionaries

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:49.040
and character encyclopedias
in parallel to our work.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.540
Because of that,
Daitokai isn't progressing at all.

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.180
It's been 13 years already.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.510
Thirteen years?!

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:01.550
We would like to make it to the end
from here.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:06.130
We are already up to our third pass
of proofreading. It's just a little more.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.560
Sensei, are you still not over your cold?

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:13.500
Yes, I'm having a bit of trouble
kicking this cold completely.

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:16.040
Please do not strain yourself.

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:19.040
I'm sorry to worry you.

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:25.210
Well, I'm going to go walk the sensei
to the station.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.150
Wait here until I get back, okay,
Kishibe-chan?

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:31.520
- I'm sorry. Thank you.
- No prob.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.700
Excuse me.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.940
Thank you so much for coming
to our restaurant today.

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:54.240
I am Majime's wife and owner
of this restaurant, Kaguya Hayashi.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.640
I am sure my husband
has been quite the handful.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.980
You're the chief's wife?!

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.080
- Yes.
- I'm Kishibe.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:09.420
Majime has been really looking forward
to you joining the dictionary team.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.260
I'm sure he might prove quite troublesome
from time to time,

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.130
but please take good care of him.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:20.000
Oh, me as well.

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:23.140
- This is pretty good.
- I tried adding ginger.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:24.500
I'm sorry.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:27.440
I don't think I can do this.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.750
I'm sorry.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:35.610
What do you mean?

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.320
The dictionary!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:42.090
My entire career,
I've worked on fashion magazines.

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:44.520
But now I suddenly have
to work on dictionaries?

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:50.160
I knew I was disliked!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.570
Every time I got criticized for an article,

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:55.100
I would complain to the editor in chief.

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:57.700
And I got into so many fights.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.170
That's why they pushed me out.

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:02.610
That's not true, Kishibe-san.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:05.480
The Northern Black editor-in-chief

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:10.080
has told me you had a certain talent
with words and that you're exceptional.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:14.690
It did seem there was some conflict
over your articles,

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:19.060
but that's because you placed a lot
of importance on the words, isn't it?

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:22.160
I placed a lot of importance on words?

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.060
Yes.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.230
That can't be true.

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:29.440
The editor-in-chief would always...

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:36.380
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to bring this up.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.280
It's okay.

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:39.780
I'm sorry!

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:43.120
- Please excuse me!
- Kishibe-san!

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.130
I couldn't get through to her.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:05.540
Even when you want to say something,
it doesn't come across...

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:10.080
Words are hard.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:15.710
But I think Kishibe-san is just like you.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:20.620
It would be nice if you could make
this dictionary together.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:23.860
Yes.

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.300
Huh? Kishibe-chan?

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:33.270
Shoot, did the welcome party end?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.340
Araki-san just goes on forever, you know?

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:40.610
Huh?

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:44.640
You place a lot of importance
on words, huh?

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:48.710
I was just doing the best I could.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:51.880
I wanted to get across
the kind of fashion I liked.

00:17:52.790 --> 00:17:55.690
But it often didn't go too well.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.690
I don't know anything anymore.

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:02.500
You used to be in the Dictionary
Editorial Department, right?

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:05.730
What does it mean
to place importance on words?

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:09.130
I have no idea.

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:15.770
Hey, so if I asked you to explain
what right is, how would you answer?

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:18.280
Right?

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.150
How would I do that?

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:22.450
Right?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:26.920
The hand you don't put
your wedding ring on or something?

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:29.820
Oh, but maybe some people
do put it on the right.

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:32.760
When you look at the northern sky,

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:36.300
it's the direction
the sun and moon rises from?

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:41.930
When you point your body to the north,

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:44.700
it's the side that is on the east!

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:47.470
How was that?

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.780
You're perfect for dictionaries.

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.350
I can guarantee you that.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.960
I'm not going to give up yet.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.330
All right, sounds good.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:22.270
To Majime, let's go drink again,
you got a good newbie.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:23.940
All right.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.950
Dictionary Editorial Department

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:28.880
- Chief, do you have a moment?
- Yes?

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.520
I had a chance to look through this.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:34.850
Would you ever consider looking
over the fashion words again?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:36.990
Some have old definitions,

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.360
and there are some recently
established words that are missing.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.460
Overall, I found it lacking.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.760
It is, isn't it?

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:49.230
Would you allow me to do this?

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.800
Please.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.580
Yes, of course.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.250
Kishibe-san, I also have a favor to ask.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:07.690
I'd like you to address me as Majime
instead of chief.

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:10.520
Oh, okay. I can do that.

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:15.790
Well, I will check this immediately,
Majime-san.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:18.800
Good.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:22.300
Compile: produce (a list or book)

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:24.870
by assembling information
collected from other sources.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.610
Hey

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:40.350
It’s a full moon tonight

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.820
I speak to you

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:51.060
Softly as you sleep

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:55.500
Your gestures

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:58.340
Attitude

00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:03.380
And way of life

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:10.020
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:15.920
So please stay the way you are

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:21.860
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:27.570
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:30.340
I’ve loved you

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:35.440
From the day

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:40.610
We met

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:50.790
Stickiness

00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:53.490
- I don't get it.
- Oh, that?

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:55.030
Nishioka-san!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.660
I mean, smart phones have that stickiness
where I can go through the screen quickly.

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:01.970
I see! So this is another stickiness too!

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.800
That's completely wrong.
